## Introduction

This document demonstrates how to generate a table of contents using the `headers` filter.

### Why Use a TOC?

A table of contents helps readers navigate longer documents quickly.

### How It Works

The `headers` filter extracts all headers from markdown content, returning a list of dictionaries with `level` and `title` keys.

## Features

### Flexible Rendering

Because `headers` returns data (not markup), you control exactly how the TOC is rendered.

### Level Filtering

Use `min_level` and `max_level` to include only certain header levels.

## Advanced Usage

### Numbered Lists

You can render the TOC as a numbered list instead of bullets.

### Custom Styling

Add CSS classes, icons, or any other markup you need.

## Conclusion

The `headers` filter provides a simple, flexible way to generate tables of contents.
